#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179465 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179626 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c6535bf-7dd1-5231-a992-9aefb8066499" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations With Unknown Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "ddcd149b-a90b-5ed2-923d-75e8a84ff145" :question/math-academy-id "e-13901" :question/problem "Solve the equation $5ky-13=7$ for the variable $y.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate $y.$ To do this, we first add $13$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5ky-13 & =7 \\\\ 5ky-13+13 & =7+13 \\\\ 5ky & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $5k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5ky & =20 \\\\ \\frac{5ky}{5k} & =\\frac{20}{5k} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{5k}y}{\\cancel{5k}} & =\\frac{20}{5k} \\\\ y & =\\frac{20}{5k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4}{5k} \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\cancel{5}\\cdot 4}{\\cancel{5}k} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4}{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179466 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179627 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aefe9086-38a5-5055-9f95-56eafacf518b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Containing Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "6eb1b4ba-3182-5ecc-8ae0-72ec27036b29" :question/math-academy-id "e-13902" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\dfrac 34 kx + 9 = 2$ for the variable $x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $4$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}kx+9 & =2 \\\\ 4\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4}kx+9) & =4\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3kx+36 & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to isolate $x.$ To do this, we first subtract $36$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3kx+36 & =8 \\\\ 3kx+36-36 & =8-36 \\\\ 3kx & =-28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $3k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3kx & =-28 \\\\ \\frac{3kx}{3k} & =\\frac{-28}{3k} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{3k}x}{\\cancel{3k}} & =\\frac{-28}{3k} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{28}{3k}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179468 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41be5b01-b9ea-576b-a7e5-d522b8b1dc88" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Using Cross Multiplication"}] :question/id #uuid "b35596e5-5914-502f-87dd-89348ab1664c" :question/math-academy-id "e-13904" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{1}{3} = -\\dfrac{ax}{5}$ for the variable $x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate $x.$ To do this, we first cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & =-\\frac{ax}{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{-ax}{5} \\\\ 5\\cdot 1 & =3\\cdot (-ax) \\\\ 5 & =-3ax\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-3a\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =-3ax \\\\ \\frac{5}{-3a} & =\\frac{-3ax}{-3a} \\\\ \\frac{5}{-3a} & =\\frac{\\cancel{-3a}x}{\\cancel{-3a}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3a} & =x \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{3a}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179627 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aefe9086-38a5-5055-9f95-56eafacf518b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Containing Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a20f6bb1-91fe-5f05-a0cd-c6a731b3cf24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487868} {:answer/id #uuid "a56f5029-2998-5dff-b344-76ca8498ecf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487874} {:answer/id #uuid "c1cb5b5d-1ea4-56fd-90f9-edec6664d770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487934} {:answer/id #uuid "d50d6314-2704-57cc-8acc-f790eb7800e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5v}{4v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487972} {:answer/id #uuid "db283fef-611c-5d11-9408-b9d041b4f5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1cb5b5d-1ea4-56fd-90f9-edec6664d770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487934} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9795343-ebe1-5a6d-9824-2c6e0c43c343" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06c556aa-e44d-528e-81fb-0f187fd8faf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-133663" :question/problem "If $\\frac{4}{3}=5vs,$ then $s=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $3$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} & =5vs \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} & =3\\cdot 5vs \\\\ 4 & =15vs\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to isolate $s.$ To do this, we divide both sides of the equation by $15v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =15vs \\\\ \\frac{4}{15v} & =\\frac{15vs}{15v} \\\\ \\frac{4}{15v} & =\\frac{\\cancel{15v}s}{\\cancel{15v}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{15v} & =s \\\\ s & =\\frac{4}{15v}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179627 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aefe9086-38a5-5055-9f95-56eafacf518b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Containing Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a54108e-6019-5a03-8ce0-8ab6c1fec0a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487620} {:answer/id #uuid "414b5a4c-65d0-557e-abcd-8e3a2ff2db10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487696} {:answer/id #uuid "4ae38b6d-4985-5481-8121-af9f93f5ab4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487713} {:answer/id #uuid "529c00d6-be9f-50e8-9c09-cf89e11a460b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487732} {:answer/id #uuid "cc20d3f7-f8d2-5d41-9c68-291c2aed5e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "529c00d6-be9f-50e8-9c09-cf89e11a460b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487732} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcffec60-3308-5f80-a86e-fd4c6b6cad44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76378346-6bd7-5f90-bb11-bc03bf523eef" :question/math-academy-id "q-133665" :question/problem "If $2=\\frac{3}{10}hk,$ then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $10$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{3}{10}hk \\\\ 10\\cdot 2 & =10\\cdot \\frac{3}{10}hk \\\\ 20 & =3hk\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to isolate $k.$ To do this, we divide both sides of the equation by $3h:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20 & =3hk \\\\ \\frac{20}{3h} & =\\frac{3hk}{3h} \\\\ \\frac{20}{3h} & =\\frac{\\cancel{3h}k}{\\cancel{3h}} \\\\ \\frac{20}{3h} & =k \\\\ k & =\\frac{20}{3h}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179626 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c6535bf-7dd1-5231-a992-9aefb8066499" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations With Unknown Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a64d3f47-43af-5127-9e4b-ae2e4dd35f66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a64d3f47-43af-5127-9e4b-ae2e4dd35f66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487878} :answer-field/id #uuid "83214493-8a7a-53b4-a9de-c3bd71553689" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b499b93-e0d8-519c-9fd8-51ac13674a1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-214556" :question/problem "If $2=-5ab,$ then $a=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate $a.$ To do this, we divide both sides of the equation by $-5b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =-5ab \\\\ \\frac{2}{-5b} & =\\frac{-5ab}{-5b} \\\\ \\frac{2}{-5b} & =\\frac{\\cancel{-5b}a}{\\cancel{-5b}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5b} & =a \\\\ a & =-\\frac{2}{5b}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179626 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c6535bf-7dd1-5231-a992-9aefb8066499" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations With Unknown Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3618254-a807-5bc1-b852-b2d8982c3e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3618254-a807-5bc1-b852-b2d8982c3e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487938} :answer-field/id #uuid "33e39e61-5c33-5c26-af08-85223061bd41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8bf4f7f2-b45d-5aef-8d47-16e8d1e1f900" :question/math-academy-id "q-214561" :question/problem "If $5=-14ab-2,$ then $a=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate $a.$ To do this, we first add $2$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =-14ab-2 \\\\ 5+2 & =-14ab-2+2 \\\\ 7 & =-14ab\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-14b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =-14ab \\\\ \\frac{7}{-14b} & =\\frac{-14ab}{-14b} \\\\ \\frac{7}{-14b} & =\\frac{\\cancel{-14b}a}{\\cancel{-14b}} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{14b} & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the right-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{7\\cdot 2b} & =a \\\\ -\\frac{\\cancel{7}}{\\cancel{7}\\cdot 2b} & =a \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2b} & =a \\\\ a & =-\\frac{1}{2b}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41be5b01-b9ea-576b-a7e5-d522b8b1dc88" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Using Cross Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148fb1e1-6469-5e9f-8607-d19a1b547d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "148fb1e1-6469-5e9f-8607-d19a1b547d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487610} :answer-field/id #uuid "4145a264-18fa-5615-9a7b-19eca3f91555" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c956651-7831-59be-948a-98c8e15c7d28" :question/math-academy-id "q-214615" :question/problem "If $-\\frac{3xy}{10}=\\frac{1}{2},$ then $y=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate $y.$ To do this, we first cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3xy}{10} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{-3xy}{10} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\cdot (-3xy) & =10\\cdot 1 \\\\ -6xy & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-6x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6xy & =10 \\\\ \\frac{-6xy}{-6x} & =\\frac{10}{-6x} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-6x}\\,y}{\\cancel{-6x}} & =\\frac{10}{-6x} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{10}{6x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the right-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{2\\cdot 5}{2\\cdot 3x} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5}{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 3x} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{5}{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41be5b01-b9ea-576b-a7e5-d522b8b1dc88" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Using Cross Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e381f39-c03c-5574-915d-4a343cc4cb78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{42n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487786} {:answer/id #uuid "aa5f1033-a8e2-5f84-88cd-f03d888abc9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{21n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487893} {:answer/id #uuid "c6610624-2863-5638-a438-3678da72f23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{42n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487944} {:answer/id #uuid "e227ad4b-5b07-5ce7-a465-4950eeef78da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{21n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488000} {:answer/id #uuid "fb43d269-818b-501a-95d5-50e37b024951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{21n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa5f1033-a8e2-5f84-88cd-f03d888abc9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{21n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487893} :answer-field/id #uuid "74722e8c-447b-54a8-a4b0-54e7b6f9a748" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "821390a9-15de-5be4-b110-42ad4543a1a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-75488" :question/problem "If $\\frac{12nx}{2}=\\frac{4}{7},$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate $x.$ To do this, we first cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12nx}{2} & =\\frac{4}{7} \\\\ 7\\cdot 12nx & =2\\cdot 4 \\\\ 84nx & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $84n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}84nx & =8 \\\\ \\frac{84nx}{84n} & =\\frac{8}{84n} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{84n}x}{\\cancel{84n}} & =\\frac{8}{84n} \\\\ x & =\\frac{8}{84n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the right-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{4\\cdot 2}{4\\cdot 21n} \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\cancel{4}\\cdot 2}{\\cancel{4}\\cdot 21n} \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{21n}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
